polyopia@gmail.com wrote:
> I've got a level one wizard who found a wand of wishing.  I know that
> I'm going to screw it up somehow, but I'd like some advice on what to
> wish for.
> 
> I already got the scroll of charging, SDSM, and boots of speed.
> 
> I'm wondering what to wish for next...
> 
> I was considering a helm of brilliance, (could easily find one in a
> shop though), a bag of holding (sokoban...), or maybe a spellbook of
> polymorph or ID.
> 

A (blessed) spellbook of ID is a wonderful wish and having everything 
ID'd will save your life many times. I would not wish for holding or 
brilliance yet if I were you; wait until minetown I'd say. You might 
consider blessed potions of gain ability; for now, they'd do you better 
than a helm of brilliance (if your INT has room to grow).

Concentrate on staying alive; any wish is useful if it helps you get to 
the castle wand. Don't worry about wishing for something that will be 
obsoleted and don't wish for something that will only be very useful 
much later.

Consider polymorph and polycontrol; Vampire Lords are great to play 
(until footrices) and you wouldn't need to fear polytraps, which can 
lead to death pretty easily. For the late (and early as well) game a 
Xorn is fantastic; Gehennom is trivial and you can always take the 
shortest path when fleeing the wizard. You also get all the intrinsics 
you could possibly want including unbreathing and stoning resistance!

I'd also consider wishing for a good artifact, particularly a quest 
artifact (wait until you have more hitpoints!). Wizards generally do 
find with MB but the Staff of Aescliopican'tspell is damn nice. By the 
time you get to the castle it's FAR harder to wish for an artifact. 
Now's the time!


